WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
1959.

2
00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:07.980
A BBC interviewer asks the Swiss
psychiatrist Carl Jung if he believes in God.

3
00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.880
Jung replies: I don't need to believe.

4
00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:12.100
I know.

5
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.150
Jung had once been
Freud's closest colleague.

6
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.170
But they split, and Jung rejected
Freud's view of religion as neurosis.

7
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.410
So could a psychologist think
religion is good for you,

8
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.940
without claiming that God exists?

9
00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:29.430
In this mission, you'll go down
through the layers of the mind,

10
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.600
to a level Jung believed all humans share.

11
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:37.220
Then you'll weigh his ideas against
critics who say they cannot be tested.

12
00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:41.710
Your mission: find out whether a
psychologist could call religion good for you

13
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.890
without claiming that God exists.
